From 365e9311be2cf3e3edee52a6f3f79b2700d89e83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gebhard <direkt@gebhardborck.de>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:33:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(worker): post-write verification, exit-code respect, no
 acceptance-anxiety blocks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three patches close the failure mode observed in t_cd4c0ae0 (developer,
blocked 2026-10-06): a worker that produced correct-looking diffs in
its conversation log but did not persist them, ignored test-runner exit
codes, and used kanban_block(needs_input) as an acceptance escape hatch.

Patches

1. Post-write verification (tools/file_tools.py). patch_tool now takes a
   content-SHA256 snapshot of every target path before and after the
   write. When the underlying file_ops backend is local the snapshot
   reads from the host; for non-local backends (Docker/SSH/Modal) the
   backend's own read_file_raw is the authoritative source. A reported
   success with an unchanged disk becomes success=False with an explicit
   'Post-write verification failed' error.

2. Exit-code respect (tools/terminal_tool_result.py). finalize_foreground_result
   classifies test-runner commands via agent.verification_evidence and
   attaches status=failed, error='failed: <tail>' whenever the runner
   exited non-zero, even if its stdout prints 'N passed' for some
   sub-runner. status=ok is reserved for exit_code == 0.

3. Block-kind guard (tools/kanban_tools.py + kanban_tools_schemas.py
   + agent/prompt_builder.py KANBAN_GUIDANCE). Dispatcher workers may
   call kanban_block with kind=needs_input only when the task body
   contains an explicit 'Question for user: <X>' or 'Frage an User: <X>'
   line and the call's reason repeats <X> exactly. Acceptance anxiety
   (Akzeptanzpunkt, please confirm, 'möchte gerne Bestätigung') is
   refused with a message that points at kanban_complete and
   kanban_request_review. The KANBAN_GUIDANCE prompt is updated in the
   same shape so workers stop attempting the escape in the first place.

Tests (all green locally with /usr/bin/git, 4 + 2 + 1 tests):

- tests/hermes_cli/test_worker_post_write_verify.py
  4 tests cover the local-success path, the local-silent-write path,
  the local-no-op path, and a host-absent / remote-backend path where
  the backend read is the authoritative snapshot.
- tests/hermes_cli/test_worker_test_exit_honored.py
  1 test asserts that exit_code=1 with stdout '4 passed' yields
  status=failed and an error string starting with 'failed:'.
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_block_guard.py
  2 tests assert that 'Akzeptanzpunkt' reason is refused and that a
  reason that exactly matches a briefed 'Frage an User:' line is
  accepted. The first test reproduces the t_cd4c0ae0 failure mode.

Anti-pattern under repair: workers that emit convincing diffs in their
conversation transcript without persisting them to disk; workers that
read test-runner stdout instead of the runner's exit code; workers
that treat the dispatcher review as a forum to renegotiate scope.

Refs: Kanban t_4c2758c2 (this card), Kanban t_cd4c0ae0 (anti-example).
